# A symmetric binding rule whose rate parameter is 0 at load, switched on by
# an RNF script. The rule's symmetry factor (0.5) must be applied to the new
# rate, as it is to a rate read at load.
#
# From 200 A(b), at kf = 0.01 and kr = 1 the system relaxes within a few time
# units to about 50 dimers. AA counts both molecules of each dimer, so it is
# about 100: a network SSA (BioNetGen 2.9.3, 200 seeds) gives 100.3 +/- 0.6 at
# t = 5, and the ODE 100. With the rule left out AA stays 0, and with the
# factor left off it is about 124.
begin model
begin parameters
  N0 200
  kf 0
  kr 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b) N0
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules AA A(b!1).A(b!1)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  dimerize: A(b) + A(b) <-> A(b!1).A(b!1) kf, kr
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
writeXML()
end actions
